/Title (Kurdish  The Kurdish people constitute a distinct Indo-European ethnic group of roughly 35 to 40 million people, split across Turkey, Syria, Iraq, and Iran following the post-WWI dissolution of the Ottoman Empire. Lacking a sovereign state, Kurdish groups have pursued autonomy or independence through both political and armed struggles. The Kurdistan Workers' Party \(PKK\) launched an armed insurgency against the Turkish state in 1984, demanding Kurdish autonomy. The conflict expanded into northern Iraq and northern Syria, where Kurdish groups established autonomous regions amid broader state instability.)
/Dest [33 0 R /Fit]
