/Title (The Red Sea conflict highlights a stark contrast in AI applications. The Houthis deploy low-cost, AI-enabled autonomous underwater vehicles \(AUVs\) and surface drones that use basic computer vision to identify the hull profiles of large ships for ramming attacks. Naval coalitions respond with highly advanced AI combat management systems, such as Aegis, which autonomously categorize, prioritize, and track hundreds of fast-moving aerial and surface threats in real-time, recommending optimal interception options to human commanders.)
