/Title (Following the 1979 Islamic Revolution, Iran adopted a staunchly anti-Zionist stance, viewing Israel as an illegitimate state and a tool of Western imperialism. For decades, the two nations engaged in a low-intensity shadow war: Iran built and funded an axis of regional proxy groups \(Hezbollah, Hamas, Houthis\), while Israel engaged in targeted assassinations of Iranian nuclear scientists and cyber-sabotage campaigns \(such as the Stuxnet virus\). This shadow war burst into the open with direct, large-scale interstate military strikes involving ballistic missiles, cruise missiles, and combat drones.)
